  {
    "episode_id": 50982,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50982.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Hello and welcome to the Byron York show the no chit chat podcast we'd like to get right into it and what we're going to get into today is a little bit different. You know over the past several weeks we talked a lot about Liz Cheney's primary race in Wyoming in which she was finally defeated in a landslide. But we haven't talked we haven't spoken to. Harriet Hageman, the woman, the Republican candidate who defeated Liz Cheney in Wyoming, and that's what we're going to do today. Fresh from her big victory in the Republican primary, she actually came to Washington to meet some people. She's actually a working lawyer on environmental cases, and she came to Washington to make an argument. One of those cases, you'll hear her describe that. So we got to sit down and talk a little bit about why she thinks she won this race, why Liz Cheney lost this race, and what she wants to do. So it's a really, really interesting conversation. We do get into the whole issue of the January 6th Committee in Donald Trump, which was the focus of Liz Cheney's single issue candidacy. And just learned a lot about Harriet Hageman and about Wyoming. So I hope you'll enjoy it. Let's listen now to my interview with Harriet Hageman. Harriet Hageman, thank you for joining us on The Byron York Show.",
