  {
    "episode_id": 50982,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50982.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "I think it demonstrates that maybe encapsulates what the campaign was about. For Liz Cheney, the campaign was about Liz Cheney. For Harriet Haggum and the campaign was about Wyoming and how we fix what's going on in this country. And why it is so Wyoming-centric for me is not only because I'm running to represent Wyoming and I'm from Wyoming. But Wyoming is the key to prosperity in this country. We're the largest coal producer in the nation. We're one of the largest oil and gas producers in the nation. We have one of the largest reserves for uranium. We're a large cattle producer. As I say, we are the ones that put food on your table, gas in your car, roof over your head, and we pave your highways. That's the kind of stuff that we do in Wyoming. And what we've seen with the Biden administration and the out of control inflation, the mess that we're seeing in Ukraine between Russia and Ukraine, the other issues that we've seen with the skyrocketing energy costs, all of those relate to really bad policies coming out of this administration, and those policies are directed at Wyoming. Wyoming is one of the largest targets of the Biden administration in terms of attempting to destroy our economy.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
