  {
    "episode_id": 50982,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50982.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 45,
    "turn_text": "Well, they say it's for traceability, but we already have traceability. And in 2013, there was a regulation. We have traceability through brands, ear tags, back tags, tattoos. We have other ways to trace cattle. And in fact, we do it very, very effectively. What this comes down to is the ear tag manufacturing companies and the four big packers on RFID. So USDA, contrary to what our cattle industry wants, adopted an RFID mandate. It's not feasible in most of the interior west of the United States. We're out in the middle of nowhere working cattle. The other thing that they required was that all of our ranchers would have to register their ranches with the federal government. What in the world would the purpose of that be? We now look at it. It's a form of surveillance. It is so that they can determine where we're moving cattle, and then start imposing restrictions on how we raise cattle",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
